          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আগেই — āgei — \"already\". It is আগে, \"before\", with the emphatic -ই: আমি আগেই খেয়েছি — āmi āgei kheyechhi — \"I have already eaten.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আগেই (āgei) is āge, \"before\", from Sanskrit agre, \"in front\" (CDIAL 68), + the stressing ending -i: \"already\"."
            }
          ]
        },
