          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কাটানো (kāṭāno) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from kartati, \"cuts\" (CDIAL 2854). Kāṭāno is the causing form of kāṭā, \"to cut\"; CDIAL lists both."
            }
          ]
        },
